## Data model (import writes)

| CSV | DB |
|-----|-----|
| `Title` | `v2_offering.name` |
| `Offering Type` | must match `--type` → `offering_type_id` |
| `Program (tag)` | `v2_category` (Learn / Explore / Compete) → `category_id` |
| `Image Link` | `poster_url` |
| `Description for admin` | `description` (admin note; ≠ `content\|description`) |
| `{group}\|{field}` | `type_config_data` nested JSON |
| (derived) | flatten `content.*` / `pricing.*` to table columns on write |

Before insert/update: merge `v2_category.config_base` into `type_config_data` (category defaults, row values win).

## Upsert keys

1. Row has `id` → UPDATE by id (id must exist).
2. No `id` → match `name` + `offering_type_id` → UPDATE or INSERT.
3. New rows: **leave `id` and `slug` empty**; slug auto-allocated on INSERT.
4. `UNCHANGED` when diff empty; `failed > 0` → exit 1.

**Guards:** no `offering_type_id` change on update; no `category_id` change if `v2_instance` references offering.

## Import logging

- **Console:** per-row `[rowNum] ACTION Title (Program) id=…`; final `Summary: { insert, update, unchanged, skipped, failed }`.
- **JSON report:** `scripts/output/import-offerings-{type}-{timestamp}.json` — `mode`, `file`, `manifest`, `schema_hash`, `drift_warnings`, `summary`, `results[]` (`action`, `id`, `slug`, `error`).
- No separate `.log` text file (unlike `import-instances.js`).

## Schema drift

Companion manifest: `{csvBasename}-schema.json`. If `schema_hash` ≠ DB → WARN, validate against live schema. After Admin edits `offering_schema`, re-run `export-offerings.js` before editing CSV.

